    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The same idea works for a quotient.\n\n√(196/4)\n= √196 / √4\n= 14/2\n= 7",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So √(x/y) = √x / √y when the roots are defined.\n\nAgain, the point is to turn one awkward-looking root into two easy ones.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_5": {
      "id": "q_5",
